// The cli module builds against the framework in this checkout: go.mod
// requires a published version of the core, which go install and go mod
// tidy use; this workspace's replace points it here instead, without a
// replace directive in go.mod, which go install refuses. A replace rather
// than "use ..": the core's go.mod is then read from the checkout, so the
// build doesn't need the required version to be published yet (a release
// commit requires the version it releases). See
// docs/contributing/releasing.md.
go 1.26.0

use .

replace anetos.dev/anetos => ..
